cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nexus ShadowBench: an open benchmark for shadow AI agent discovery"
message: >-
  If you use Nexus ShadowBench, its corpora or its results, please cite
  this repository together with the commit and results directory you used.
  The corpora and labels are author-written and not independent; quote
  results with the caveats in the README.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Nexus ShadowScan contributors
    website: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-ShadowBench
repository-code: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-ShadowBench
url: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-ShadowBench/tree/main/docs
abstract: >-
  ShadowBench measures whether discovery tools find AI agents and plain
  AI use across nine surfaces (code, identity, LLM gateways, low-code,
  SaaS, cloud, endpoints, network and runtime) without flagging look-alike
  decoys. It holds a generated cases track, an authored whole-organization
  estate track and a code-surface track over pinned public repositories,
  with tool-neutral ground truth, fail-closed scoring, confidence intervals,
  paired tests and SHA-256 provenance for every input and recorded run.
keywords:
  - shadow-ai
  - ai-agents
  - benchmark
  - agent-discovery
  - mcp
  - security
  - ai-inventory
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: Nexus ShadowScan
    authors:
      - name: Nexus ShadowScan contributors
    repository-code: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-ShadowScan
    version: 0.1.2
